title ALES159 — Lotus's stereo_expand: the downward expander carried into stereo, the gate's linked decision fused with the compressor's linked gain — completing the core stereo dynamics quartet
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Fourth rung this turn (after ALES156 gate, ALES157 compress, ALES158 limit — all sent). The expander (ALES60) is the fourth mono dynamics member, the one that makes the family symmetric (softens the gate's hard floor, continuous at the threshold). Carrying it to stereo completes the core stereo dynamics quartet, and it is the rung that FUSES the two linking laws the family has proven separately.
think Two truths meet, and this is the crux. (1) The decision must be linked, like the gate (ALES156): the expander pushes DOWN the quiet, so expanding each channel by whether IT alone is below threshold would push the quiet right down while the loud left plays — the gate's image-tear bug. So a pair is expanded iff BOTH below (key = max(|L|,|R|) < thr). (2) The gain must be linked, like the compressor (ALES157): the widened factor max(0, thr - deficit*ratio)/m is magnitude-dependent, so expanding each channel by its own deficit gives different gains and shifts the image. So one gain from the linked key applied to both. No prior single rung needed BOTH linkings at once; the expander does, which is why it is the honest completion of the arc.
think Careful edges: key==0 (both silent) must be guarded before the divide (silence stays silence, no div-by-zero) — added a key>0 branch. new_key = max(0, thr - (thr-key)*num/den), floored at silence (the gate reached from within). The louder-quiet channel (|x|=key) lands on new_key = mono expand(key); the quieter channel scaled by new_key/key. Overflow: |sample|*new_key <= 32768*32768 fits i64; new_key<=key so quotient<=|sample| fits i16.
think Five laws witnessed first-try GREEN: linked decision+gain (left-always-peak master: left'=mono expand(left) {0,-600,2000,0}, right scaled same fraction {0,-300,1500,0}, independent mono expand(right)={0,0,1500,0} shown to differ at idx1), image (no expand/flip, out-of-phase quiet pair stays out of phase {600,-200,800,0}, loud pair passes whole), at-threshold (keys>=thr identity, continuous), knob laws (unit ratio identity, higher ratio monotone, huge ratio silences a quiet pair), silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate (all-silent stays zero via key=0 guard, length held, four refusals untouched+balanced, count0 identity).
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, values only, one multiply-then-divide per channel per sample, memoryless, a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, TAME bans clean, no red. The core stereo dynamics quartet is now whole: stereo_gate (links decision), stereo_compress (links gain), stereo_limit (compressor ratio->inf, brickwall+image), stereo_expand (fuses both linkings). Recorded lesson: the family teaches one arc in four rungs — a stereo dynamics processor links the DECISION when its below/above gain is constant (gate), links the GAIN when its gain is magnitude-dependent (compressor/limiter), and links BOTH when it is a magnitude-dependent processor that acts on the QUIET side (expander). The natural next members are the ENVELOPE-following (attack/release) dynamics (ALES52-62) carried to stereo — those add CARRIED STATE per channel (a per-channel envelope memory) atop the linked detector, a new stereo shape (linked detector feeding a shared or per-channel envelope). Front doors synced in the same commit.
loom witness=ales_stereo_expand_witness result=GREEN laws=linked-decision+gain+image+at-threshold+knobs+silence/balance channels=2 class=stereo-dynamics-fuses-both-linkings detector=linked-max(|L|,|R|) expand-iff=both-below-threshold gain=new_key/key-shared new_key=max(0,thr-(thr-key)*num/den) cases=linked(left-always-peak:left'=mono-expand(left){0,-600,2000,0},right-same-fraction{0,-300,1500,0},independent-mono-right{0,0,1500,0}-differs-idx1)+image(no-expand/flip,out-of-phase-quiet-stays{600,-200,800,0},loud-pair-whole)+at-threshold(keys>=thr-identity)+knobs(unit-ratio-identity,higher-monotone,huge-silences)+silence(all-zero-via-key0-guard)+balance/atomicity(4-refusals-untouched-balanced,count0-identity) reds=0 quartet=gate+compress+limit+expand-whole
file lotus/stereo_expand.rye ALES159 — stereo_expand, the downward expander lifted to stereo by FUSING the linked decision (a pair expanded iff both below thr) with the linked gain (both scaled by new_key/key from the linked max); key=0 guarded; StereoExpandError = ALES60's ExpandError reused whole; completes the core stereo dynamics quartet.
